    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d786">

                <pb facs="0873" n="679" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv02/pg679"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 EAC/7–2745: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 786<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                        Political Adviser to the Representative on the European Advisory
                        Commission</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Mosely</hi>)<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d786-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-07-27T20:00:00+01:00">July 27, 1945—8 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>French representative<anchor n="2" xml:id="d786-f2"/> in letter July 16 informed
                    me his government’s approval agreement on zones occupation Austria and its
                    covering report as reported my telegram to Dept 7205 July 17,<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d786-f3"/> repeated AusPolAd as 24 and Frankfurt for Murphy and
                    Mosely as 40.</p>
                <p>EAC (European Advisory Committee) this evening approved texts summaries of
                    agreements on zones occupation and control machinery Austria and agreed present
                    them next Tuesday to representatives other Allied governments including
                    representative new Polish Government. Summary of control machinery agreement is
                    brief and contains no mention names of MG (Military Government) divisions.</p>
                <p>Sent Babelsberg for Mosely Secret from Winant and to Dept July 27, <hi
                        rendition="#small-caps">Comea</hi> 344.</p>
                <p>US, UK and French representatives are ready to recommend that these summaries
                    together with statement on consultation with other United Nations governments re
                    Austria be published simultaneously as joint statements in four capitals. Soviet
                        representative<anchor n="4" xml:id="d786-f4"/> also agrees but must first
                    obtain his government’s approval of texts. At my suggestion to expedite approval
                    US, UK and Soviet representatives are transmitting texts these three statements
                    to Potsdam and French representative transmitting texts to Paris. Publication
                    date can be arranged upon approval by all four governments.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Winant</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
